  "summary": {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "variant": "lead",
    "children": [
      {
        "text": "Panagsama Beach is the main beach of Moalboal in southwestern Cebu, lined with dive resorts and restaurants. Swim out from the shore and you can see a school of sardines and a coral drop-off. Its relaxed backpacker feel is a big part of the appeal."
      }
    ]
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "section",
      "key": "overview",
      "title": "At a glance",
      "icon": "info",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Panagsama Beach is a beach in Barangay Basdiot in the municipality of Moalboal, on the southwestern coast of Cebu Island. Wikipedia says most of Moalboal's resorts and restaurants are concentrated here. Wikivoyage calls it a haven for snorkeling and diving and describes a place where dive resorts, schools, restaurants and nightlife sit side by side. The sand strip is narrow and the bottom is somewhat rocky, so it is less a swimming beach than a town built around what lies underwater. It is about "
            },
            {
              "type": "distance",
              "text": "3.5km"
            },
            {
              "text": " from the main bus stop in Moalboal town."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "What makes it famous is the underwater terrain that starts right off the shore. In front of the beach is a coral drop-off where the bottom falls away steeply, and according to Wikivoyage you only need to swim about "
            },
            {
              "type": "distance",
              "text": "20–30m"
            },
            {
              "text": " out to reach the edge and see the sardines. The drop-off reaches depths of "
            },
            {
              "type": "distance",
              "text": "70m"
            },
            {
              "text": ", and jacks and tuna sometimes come in to hunt the sardines. The fact that you can see all this without boarding a boat is why Panagsama is known to divers and snorkelers around the world."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "About "
            },
            {
              "type": "distance",
              "text": "3km"
            },
            {
              "text": " offshore lies Pescador Island. The municipality of Moalboal declared it a marine park and fish sanctuary in 1990, and an open-top underwater cave on its west side, nicknamed \"the Cathedral,\" made it the signature dive trip. Behind the beach, the road is lined with local eateries, convenience stores and hostels, so everything is within walking distance. Wikipedia reports that dive shops pay the municipality a fee for each diver they bring to Pescador Island, and that the money goes to patrols, waste management, and reef and mangrove rehabilitation. So part of the cost of a boat dive goes toward protecting the site."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Wikipedia reports that in 2024 Condé Nast Traveler named it one of the best beaches in Southeast Asia. Rankings differ from outlet to outlet, so take that as a rough guide only. This guide centers on the seaside strip of Panagsama but also explains how to link it with Moalboal's other sights nearby. Most prices come from older Wikivoyage figures, so check them again locally. The San Juan Nepomuceno parish of Moalboal was established on February 6, 1852, and the town became an independent municipality in 1917. In World War II, Japanese forces burned much of the town in retaliation for a guerrilla ambush, and the Japanese surrender at the Battle of Tomonoy took place on August 13, 1944. That history lies behind today's beach resort."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "key": "highlights",
      "title": "Top things to do",
      "icon": "star",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "grid",
          "columns": 2,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "card",
              "number": 1,
              "title": "Snorkeling with the shoreline sardines",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Swim out about "
                },
                {
                  "type": "distance",
                  "text": "20–30m"
                },
                {
                  "text": " from the beach and you can reportedly see a cloud of sardines at the edge of the coral drop-off. The school left after the February 2012 earthquake and returned in May 2013. Its position and size change from year to year, so ask a local shop first."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "card",
              "number": 2,
              "title": "The coral drop-off",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Close to shore the bottom plunges steeply, with many reefs especially toward the south. You can see hard and soft corals and many kinds of fish, including lionfish and sea snakes, and sometimes turtles."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "card",
              "number": 3,
              "title": "Diving at Pescador Island",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "This limestone island about "
                },
                {
                  "type": "distance",
                  "text": "3km"
                },
                {
                  "text": " off the Basdiot coast is Moalboal's signature dive site. Many trips start at the south end and drift with the current along the east or west side, and visibility can reach about "
                },
                {
                  "type": "distance",
                  "text": "40m"
                },
                {
                  "text": " on a good day. The underwater cave called \"the Cathedral\" is on the west side. The reef has a sandy slope with soft coral at 5–10 m, below which a hard-coral wall continues down to about "
                },
                {
                  "type": "distance",
                  "text": "40m"
                },
                {
                  "text": "."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "card",
              "number": 4,
              "title": "Turtles at Tongo Point",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Tongo Point is known for turtles that often appear close to shore. It is in front of Pescadores Seaview Suites. Do not touch or chase the turtles, and keep your distance."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "card",
              "number": 5,
              "title": "Dive courses and fun dives",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "The town has many PADI and SSI shops. According to Wikivoyage, one dive costs about "
                },
                {
                  "type": "price",
                  "text": "₱1,500"
                },
                {
                  "text": " with gear, locally owned shops charge "
                },
                {
                  "type": "price",
                  "text": "₱1,100–1,200"
                },
                {
                  "text": ", and three dives a day is the usual schedule. A beginner course takes about "
                },
                {
                  "type": "duration",
                  "text": "4 days"
                },
                {
                  "text": " and costs "
                },
                {
                  "type": "price",
                  "text": "₱14,500–19,000"
                },
                {
                  "text": "."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "card",
              "number": 6,
              "title": "A trip to White Beach",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Farther north in Basdako are two white-sand beaches that suit sunbathing and swimming. A motorbike taxi between Panagsama and White Beach was reported at about "
                },
                {
                  "type": "price",
                  "text": "₱150"
                },
                {
                  "text": ". Check entrance fees on site."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "card",
              "number": 7,
              "title": "Day trip to Kawasan Falls",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Wikipedia puts Kawasan Falls about "
                },
                {
                  "type": "distance",
                  "text": "20km"
                },
                {
                  "text": " from Moalboal. Wikivoyage says the walk to the falls is easy and a guide is not required, so you can politely decline guide offers."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "card",
              "number": 8,
              "title": "Evening on the beach road",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "At dusk the restaurants and bars along the beach road light up. Wikivoyage says Panagsama has a concentration of lodging, restaurants and nightlife. Late evenings can be noisy, so choose your accommodation carefully."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "key": "itinerary",
      "title": "Suggested itinerary",
      "icon": "event_note",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "tabs",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "Day plan",
              "subtitle": "Sardine snorkeling and lunch",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "stepper",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "time": "08:00",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "Rent snorkeling gear from your lodging or the beach, and check the safety rules with the shop."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "time": "08:30",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "Swim out from the shore and look for the sardine school at the coral drop-off. Do not push yourself on days with strong currents."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "time": "11:00",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "Have lunch at a local eatery on the beach road. Wikivoyage reports that meals at local eateries cost about "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "price",
                          "text": "₱80–100"
                        },
                        {
                          "text": " (2019)."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "time": "13:30",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "Walk toward Tongo Point and look for sea turtles."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "time": "16:00",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "Relax at a beach café and have dinner after sunset."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "The schedule is only an example. On windy or rough days, cut back on shore entries and follow your shop's advice."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Two-day dive plan",
              "subtitle": "Including Pescador Island",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "stepper",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "time": "Day 1, morning",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "Leave Cebu City, arrive in Moalboal and drop your bags at your lodging."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "time": "Day 1, afternoon",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "Ease in with sardine snorkeling or an intro dive, then rest early."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "time": "Day 2, morning",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "Dive at Pescador Island with a shop. Only people trained in cave diving should enter the cave section."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "time": "Day 2, afternoon",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "Check the no-fly rules after diving, then travel on."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
