    {
      "type": "section",
      "key": "stay_and_food",
      "title": "Where to stay & eat",
      "icon": "restaurant",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Wikivoyage lists backpacker options such as Moalboal Backpacker Lodge (about ₱250–850), Babu Backpackers Inn (about ₱250 per person), MoHo Moalboal Hostel (₱250 fan, ₱300 air-conditioned) and Le Village Hostel (about ₱350 per person). In the mid-range are Mayas Native Garden (from ₱800), Pescadores Seaview Suites (from ₱1,950 for two with breakfast) and Quo Vadis Dive Resort (₱1,275–3,600). Prices vary by season, so confirm them when you book."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Local eateries and restaurants cluster along the beach road. Food Stop serves generous Filipino and Asian dishes for about ₱150, and Venz Kitchen is so popular that you should arrive early or expect to queue. A 24-hour 7-Eleven makes it easy to buy snacks and water."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "key": "tips",
      "title": "Travel tips",
      "icon": "lightbulb",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "icon": "check_circle",
          "items": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "For sardine snorkeling, check the life vest and entry point with your shop first and go in with a companion."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Do not step on or touch the coral, and use reef-friendly sunscreen."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "The beach road is narrow, so leave big bags at your lodging and travel light."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "If you fly out the same day after diving, ask your shop about the required wait before flying."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Dorm beds and dive packages fill up quickly in peak season, so book ahead."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "When taking a bus, confirm the destination, ask the fare in advance and carry small change."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Bring plenty of cash. Foreign cards reportedly carry an ATM fee of about ₱250 and a limit of ₱10,000 per withdrawal."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Touts offering Kawasan Falls guides work around town. The path is easy, so agree on a price on the spot if you want one."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "key": "cautions",
      "title": "Precautions",
      "icon": "warning",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "alert",
          "variant": "warning",
          "icon": "warning",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Do not enter Pescador Island's \"Cathedral\" cave with only an open-water certification. Only people trained in cave diving should go in."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "icon": "error",
          "items": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "The beach is somewhat rocky, so water shoes are safer than flip-flops."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "ATMs are reportedly more likely to be out of order on Sundays, so get cash in advance."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Ticket collectors are reported to overcharge sometimes, so confirm the fare before boarding."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Currents can run at the sardine site, so do not swim far out alone."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
